      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nWhen using the rust frontend, if model tag points to object storage (eg S3), vllm serve fails at startup. This is bc the Rust frontend tries to resolve the path as a HF repo id, which returns 404.\r\n\r\n`ModelConfig.maybe_pull_model_tokenizer_for_runai` already pulls the config and\r\ntokenizer files into a local directory and sets `model_config.model` to it. The\r\nweights keep streaming from `model_config.model_weights`. But\r\n`RustFrontendProcessManager` builds `model_tag` from the raw CLI args, so the\r\nRust frontend never sees the local directory.\r\n\r\nSo we pass `vllm_config.model_config` to `RustFrontendProcessManager`. For\r\nobject storage models, it forwards the pulled directory as `model_tag`. Unless\r\n`--served-model-name` was given, it also sets `served_model_name` to the\r\noriginal URI, so the served model name matches the Python frontend's.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n```\r\npytest tests/entrypoints/launchers/api_server/test_api_server_process_manager.py\r\n```\r\n\r\nNew test: `test_rust_frontend_uses_pulled_object_storage_model`. It covers the\r\ndefault served name and an explicit `--served-model-name`.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\nAll 14 tests in the file pass locally.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to investigate the issue and draft this\r\nchange. I have reviewed every changed line.\r\n",
